course: dictionary
lesson: 1250
title: Reading clues about a food word
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A burger is a flat, round cake of minced meat, usually beef, cooked and served in a bread bun. A veggie burger or fish burger is a similar patty made from other foods. The words around a word give you clues: «Dad puts his burger down» tells you a burger is something you hold and eat.
explain: Clue words can also show you what a word does not mean. «A pet flytrap needs bright sun, wet soil, rainwater... and never pieces of burger, whose fat it cannot digest.» A plant that feeds on insects is not going to feed on burger, so burger must be a food for people. Always test your meaning: put it in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Some words have a story behind them. «Hamburger» comes from Hamburg, a city in Germany, not from ham, although people sometimes split it into "ham" and "burger". That is why you should check a word in a dictionary when the clues do not settle it.
fact: A burger is a flat, round patty, usually of meat, served in a bread bun.
fact: A veggie burger, chicken burger or fish burger is a similar patty made from other foods.
fact: «Hamburger» comes from Hamburg, a city in Germany.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «burger and chips», «veggie burger» and «burger bun».
fact: Meat burgers must be cooked all the way through to kill germs.
exercise: «Dad puts his burger down: "Out of order, Phil."» What is a burger? | A type of umbrella | *A flat round patty of food, served in a bun | A short song | A kind of car engine
exercise: Ella says a veggie burger must have meat in it. Is she right? | Yes, every burger is made from beef | Yes, but only if it is cooked | *No, a veggie burger is a patty made from other foods | No, because it has no bun
exercise: Why must meat burgers be cooked all the way through? | To stop them being flat | To make them bigger | To make them go soft | *To kill germs
test: «A pet flytrap needs... never pieces of burger, whose fat it cannot digest, so the trap may rot.» Why should you never feed burger to a pet flytrap? | It needs burger to stay in the sun | *It cannot digest the fat, so the trap may rot | It is too small to eat anything | It likes the taste and grows faster
test: Which phrase means a burger served with chips? | Burger bun | *Burger and chips | Hamburg | Veggie burger
exam: Which sentence is true about the word burger? | It is a kind of bread that never has a filling | It is the name of a flytrap | It is a city in Germany | *It is a flat round patty, usually of meat, served in a bun
